invariant: INV-14
file: srv_resume.c
catches: srv_flight_test
reason: a server with no clock issues and accepts tickets. With an instant
  of 0 it writes 0 as every ticket's instant, and a later server with a
  clock judges those tickets as issued at its epoch, which is decades
  stale or, on a clock that counts from boot, fresh for a week after every
  boot. cfg.h makes a missing clock mean no tickets.
  test/srv_resume_tests.h clears the instant and requires that nothing is
  sent.
--- old
    return t->cfg.srv.ticket_key != NULL && t->now_seconds != 0;
--- new
    return t->cfg.srv.ticket_key != NULL;
